	Tooltip:
		'''
		A purple mushroom species that emits a weirdly sweet smell, 
		breathing in too much of it can result in hallucinations.
		'''
}

Rainbow: {
	DisplayName: Prismatic Lightcap
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Extremely rare mushroom species that only the most dedicated mushroom hunters can find. 
		It has great adaptability and can be used for almost anything.
		'''
}

Red: {
	DisplayName: Devilscap
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A red hot spicy mushroom with horn-like protrusions on its cap,
		the stem looks like a devil's tail if uprooted.
		'''
}

Yellow: {
	DisplayName: Moldy Giantslayer
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A sickly yellow mushroom who's smell can knock out the largest predator. 
		Besides that, it tastes very good.
		'''
}

HeartyTruffle: {
	DisplayName: Heart of the Monarch
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Healing Potions are 25% less effective
		While inflicted with Potion Sickness, life regeneration is nullified
		During that time period, damage done to you will be collected
		When Potion Sickness ends, 
		you will be healed by a quarter of the collected damage instantly
		'''
}

RealityBendingShroom: {
	DisplayName: Reality-Bending Mushroom
	Tooltip:
		'''
		An otherworldly mushroom that seems to distort space-time around it.
		Just holding this in your hand makes you uncomfortable,
		maybe you aren't worthy enough to bathe in its presence.
		Deadly Dappercap might be interested in this.
		'''
}

Mushrune: {
	DisplayName: Ethereal Mushrune
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A mushroom shaped object, consisting of dark energy, it has a cosmic rune embedded into it.
		Consume to increase maximum mana by 50
		Only one may be used
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		Mushrooms are said to be cosmic anchors by truth seekers only,
		despite their somewhat bland and meaningless look, 
		they tell stories from beyond and further.
		The Ethereal Eye that is radiating from this rune is the sign of the Cosmic Keeper,
		a unique individual who can hear the fungi.
		He who sees the blood, 
		who speaks in foreign words even higher beings cannot comprehend.
		'''
}

MushroomBlockWall: {
	DisplayName: Red Mushroom Wall
	Tooltip: ""
}

ConfusingMushroom: {
	DisplayName: Overgrown Ring
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Draws the attention of the glowing royalty
		Can only be used in a Glowing Mushroom Biome
		Non-consumable
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		A ring made of pure gold that is covered in glowing mushmatter.
		It has inscriptions on it which spell the name 'Umos'.
		'''
}

RottenMemory: {
	DisplayName: Rotten Memory
	Tooltip:
		'''
		The memory of a past life, the rotting corpse of what once was.
		A life before its independence existed
		'''
}

TheDapperCap: {
	DisplayName: The Dapper Cap
	Tooltip: A stylish mushroom cap only worn by the coolest fun guys
	Lore:
		'''
		It was said that on a sunny day when the glowing royalty visited the scarlet monarch,
		a mushling was struck with will and so became its own being.
		'''
}

TheStem: {
	DisplayName: The Stem
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Using a mana potion activates Indigo Injection
		Indigo Injection disables mana consumption for 6 seconds
		Mana Sickness also has no effect during this time period
		After the effect ends, there is a 2 minute cooldown
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		A mushroom parasite that formed from a brainstem, it clings to its host.
		It formed inside the glowing royalty,
		as a means to deepen its connection to its light.
		'''
}

FungusBag: {
	DisplayName: Treasure Bag (Feudal Fungus)
	Tooltip: Right-click to open
}

RadianceTalisman: {
	DisplayName: Radiance Talisman
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons a Praying Mushroom sentry at the cursor position which creates an aura around it
		The aura increases summon damage by 5% and enemies have a 10% chance to drop a mana star upon being hit by a minion
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		When in doubt or despair, the glowing fungi can turn towards the light and pray,
		pray for safety, pray for continued fortune.
		Their very own light is what shines in the dark caverns, the light from within,
		the light from beyond, the light of freedom.
		The scarlet fungi do not share this light, only one and its kin have ever enjoyed its warm radiance.
		'''
}

GlowingMushiumBar: {
	DisplayName: Glowing Mushium Bar
	Tooltip: May cause hallucinations
}

MushiumBar: {
	DisplayName: Mushium Bar
	Tooltip: Made with love and mushrooms
}

UmosShower: {
	DisplayName: Umos Light Shower
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hold a book above your head to release continuous waves of glowing shots upwards
		Falling below 50% health empowers the shots greatly
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		A prayer book that is covered in glowing fungi and mycelium, due to its bad condition, barely anything is readable.
		'Living in the radiant light, under its warm veil you will find salvation.'
		'''
}

SusGlowsporeBag: {
	DisplayName: Suspicious Glowing Spore Bag
	Tooltip: Summons the Feudal Bab
}

FungusMask: {
	DisplayName: Feudal Fungus Mask
	Tooltip: Be the coolest fungus around
}

MushiumHat: {
	DisplayName: Twinned Ruler Cap
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Increases max life by 5
		Increases max mana by 10
		Increases damage by 2%
		'''
}

MushiumPants: {
	DisplayName: Twinned Ruler Legs
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Increases max life by 5
		Increases max mana by 10
		Increases damage by 3%
		'''
}

MushiumShirt: {
	DisplayName: Twinned Ruler Body
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Increases max life by 5
		Increases max mana by 10
		Increases damage by 3%
		'''
}

ToadLeg: {
	DisplayName: Truffle Leg
	Tooltip:
		'''
		The severed leg of a Truffle Toad, now freed from its restraints,
		it grants a powerful leap
		Double tap up to leap
		You cannot do another leap for 30 seconds
		Negates fall damage
		'''
}

RoyalFungarang: {
	DisplayName: Royal Fungarang
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Every 4th throw imbues the weapon with your life
		Imbued projectiles deal more damage and are faster
		If you had 100 mana during the throw, 
		the weapon will be boosted further and you lose that amount of mana
		'''
}

UnitedString: {
	DisplayName: United String
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Shoots Bloodshroom Arrows at the cost of 10 HP
		When a Bloodshroom Arrow hits an enemy, you get healed by 5 HP
		Right clicking will fire a Lightshroom Arrow that costs 40 mana
		Lightshroom Arrows are shot much quicker than Bloodshroom Arrows
		'''
}

UmosForce: {
	DisplayName: Umos Light Force
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Fires a green sphere of light upwards that then flies towards the cursor
		While the sphere is at the cursor position it will fire several Radiance Shots upwards
		If you hold the sphere close to you, you will gain increased life regeneration
		The sphere will not fire anything as long as it is close to you
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		A previous unreadable page has been revealed due to the now glowing texts
		'The sleeping light, we defend with all our might,
		one day it may awake, undo all that's in its wake,
		we follow and move on, the marsh into oblivion.
		'''
}

EntwinedTalisman: {
	DisplayName: Talisman of the Entwined
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons two entwined Praying Mushrooms as a sentry at the cursor position which create an aura around it
		The aura increases summon damage by 8% and enemies have a 10% chance to drop a mana star,
		and a 5% chance to drop a heart upon being hit by a minion
		'''
	Lore:
		'''
		Due to not being blessed by the light, the scarlet fungi neither glow nor do they have much consciousness
		Though sometimes, glowing mushrooms will try to become one with them,
		all in hopes of sharing their light.
		It is unknown if it actually works this way, only those who can understand their thoughts may know.
		'''
}

